s)** — KontRASt program.\n- **BI 1823911 (Boehringer Ingelheim)** — including combination with the SOS1 inhibitor BI 1701963.\n- **China-approved/China-developed**: fulzerasib (GFH925/IBI351), glecirasib (JAB-21822, Jacobio), garsorasib (D-1553, InventisBio), D3S-001 (D3 Bio).\n\nThe dominant current theme is movement from later-line monotherapy into **first-line combinations** (with anti-PD-1, with EGFR antibodies in CRC, and with SHP2/SOS1 inhibitors to blunt adaptive resistance).\n\n## ANSWER\n\nYes — the KRAS G12C inhibitor space has many active trials, but **I could not verify this with a tool**: this session has only Galaxy bioinformatics tools, no clinical-trial registry or web access, so the following is from my knowledge (cutoff May 2026) and the NCT numbers are recalled, not retrieved.\n\n- **Approved, with ongoing trials**: sotorasib (CodeBreaK 100/200/300/201/202) and adagrasib (KRYSTAL-1/-7/-10/-12).\n- **Investigational**: divarasib (KRASCENDO), olomorasib (SUNRAY-01), elironrasib/RMC-6291, MK-1084, opnurasib/JDQ443, BI 1823911, plus fulzerasib, glecirasib, garsorasib and D3S-001.\n\nVerify current recruitment status at clinicaltrials.gov searching `KRAS G12C`.","ttft_ms":3476,"ttft_stream_ms":2963,"time_to_request_ms":14,"type":"result","duration_ms":58770,"uuid":"29270e97-4f17-46c9-aedf-50ce2c833030"}